AlgebraicGeometry/AbelianVarieties/Homomorphism/EndLimit.lean
--------------------------------------------------------------
Goal: End⁰ (A ⊗ₛ K) is the colimit of End⁰ (A ⊗ₛ L) over the intermediate
fields L of K/K₀ that are finite over K₀. The functor RatEnd (over all
intermediate fields) and its cocone limitRatEnd are done; RatEndFin /
limitRatEndFin restrict them to {L // FiniteDimensional K₀ L} (via
Monotone.functor and Cocone.whisker).
[ ] limitRatEnd.isColimit : Limits.IsColimit (limitRatEndFin A K)    (l.99)
      `sorry`. Needs "spreading out" of endomorphisms (every endomorphism
      of A ⊗ₛ K is defined over a finite L). There is no assumption on
      K/K₀ at the moment (IsGalois was removed; it is not needed; see the
      note above the def, l.92–96). Without `Algebra.IsAlgebraic K₀ K` the
      statement is still true, but only via Chow's rigidity theorem (not
      in Mathlib); with it, spreading out suffices.
      Useful: Types.FilteredColimit.isColimit_eq_iff',
      isColimitOfPreserves (forget RingCat) (injectivity of the cocone maps).
[ ] Remaining refactor: use CMStructure.basechange' / Iso.basechangeTrans
      (Defn.lean) instead of the hand-built ι'', ι₀, P₁, P₂ in
      Theorem.lean (l.61–84).
[ ] Module docstring (l.12–14) still says "colimit over
      L : IntermediateField K₀ K"; it is now over the finite ones.


