[ ] topologicalKrullDim_eq_finrank_Lie                               (l.110)
      dim G = finrank (κ_ G) (Lie G). Currently `sorry`; it is used
      (e.g. in Defn.lean, l.256) only to know that dim A is finite, which
      is far stronger than needed. Note in the file: move the finiteness
      of the dimension (and commutativity) to a separate `Basic.lean`, or
      get finiteness from the CM structure (finrank_of_CM_field).
[ ] Module docstring ("Dimension of a group scheme") is a placeholder.
      Intended: dim of a group scheme, e.g. via dim of Lie G / the local
      ring at e (needed for step 1 of CMType).
[ ] Strategy Steps A + B: dim Lie G = n for G SmoothOfRelativeDimension n.
      A: m/m² ≅ κ ⊗ Ω[A⁄K] since e is K-rational
      (kerCotangentToTensor, exact_kerCotangentToTensor_mapBaseChange,
      retractionKerCotangentToTensorEquivSection). B: Ω free of rank n.
      Missing: the scheme-level glue (affine open around e → stalk).
      Note: smooth_of_grpObj gives Smooth, not SmoothOfRelativeDimension n;
      n has to be fixed near e.
[ ] Strategy Step C: ringKrullDim 𝒪_{G,e} = n (≤ is free; ≥ needs
      dimension theory of smooth/étale algebras, not in Mathlib). Gives
      regularity and dim Lie G = topologicalKrullDim G (with homogeneity).
[ ] smooth_of_grpObj (only a #check, l.43) is for GrpObj; additivize with
      to_additive as in IntHom.lean to use it for AddGrpObj.
